-- NORM-LOG N10 goal A: passed deadlines settle in order of effective instant (NORM-LOG-SPEC :335).
-- Pass: both orders FULFILLED; P is late at 2 and Q at 4, so the status a reader sees at 11 is "Q late".
-- Before A, (b RAND a) left the reader waiting.
IMPORT prelude
DECLARE Who IS ONE OF P, Q, R
DECLARE Act IS ONE OF x, y, z
GIVETH DEONTIC Who Act
a MEANS PARTY P MUST x WITHIN 2 LEST COMMIT `status` IS "P late" HENCE FULFILLED
GIVETH DEONTIC Who Act
b MEANS PARTY Q MUST y WITHIN 4 LEST COMMIT `status` IS "Q late" HENCE FULFILLED
-- one event at 10 reveals both misses; which status does a reader at 11 see?
GIVETH DEONTIC Who Act
reader MEANS PARTY R MAY z PROVIDED RECALL OFFICIAL's `status` EQUALS JUST "Q late" WITHIN 20
#TRACE (a RAND b) RAND reader AT 0 WITH (`WAIT UNTIL` 10) PARTY R DOES z AT 11
#TRACE (b RAND a) RAND reader AT 0 WITH (`WAIT UNTIL` 10) PARTY R DOES z AT 11
